                            <comment id="497062" author="emoly.liu" created="Tue, 30 Jun 2026 01:59:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;After spending some time in debugging this issue, I find it&apos;s related to TCU compensation rounding, data caching, statfs caching and statfs max_age. The calculation in &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20024&quot; title=&quot;TCU: Space accounting with Trash Can enabled is not correct&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20024&quot;&gt;LU-20024&lt;/a&gt; is correct, so this issue looks more like a testing issue. So far, I can make it pass Maloo testing with necessary data sync and wait. I will upload the patch later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;BTW, the latest debugging results with ONLY_REPEAT=50 at &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/3707e571-88ce-4b84-8360-5256f9701941.&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/3707e571-88ce-4b84-8360-5256f9701941 &lt;/a&gt;shows that &quot;lfs df&quot; and &quot;lfs df --trash&quot; can reflect the dd data size correctly every time, but the used diff between the first 10 runs keeps 8K, then no change. I can&apos;t tell where the 8K difference comes from, still need more investigation.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="501240" author="emoly.liu" created="Tue, 8 Sep 2026 13:07:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This patch can be moved to the next phase.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="503177" author="qian_wc" created="Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:50:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The fix is included in &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/ex/lustre-release/+/66544&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/ex/lustre-release/+/66544&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
